{
  "about": "Plan of 150 Days of System Design on @systemdesign.learnvora: one idea per day, in this order, 12 phases from one request to the interview capstone. Titles are checklist names of well-known ideas and designs: scripts, numbers and examples are written fresh from fetched sources, never copied from another channel, book or course. The owner decides changes to this file (2026-10-18: first draft, for approval).",
  "rules": [
    "Day N is item id s + N in three digits (Day 7 = s007). Days are made in order; none is skipped without the owner.",
    "Each reel is stand-alone: one idea, terms defined inside it, the day is only a label on the cover and in the caption. The order is a ladder (a day leans on earlier days only for background), so any day can still be watched first.",
    "A day is done when its reel is published (status done); in_progress when planned or built.",
    "formats: concept, component, pattern, trade-off, case-study, recap. level (easy, medium, hard) only for case-study days and it counts the moving parts of the design, not its prestige.",
    "Case-study titles are generic and every design is told as 'a typical design' (numbers are EXAMPLE with the arithmetic shown, unless a fetched page gives them). A real company's or a published standard's own design is only told on a source-gated day, and only after the researcher has fetched a primary source (the company's engineering post, an official incident report, the standard's own document): the reel then says only what that page says and names it on screen as 'Source: <site>'. Source-gated days: Day 112 (the outage post-mortem is chosen from a fetched official post-mortem; none fetched, the day waits or becomes 'a typical outage') and Day 137 (UPI-style payment: what the official documents say, else 'a typical design'). Any other day that wants a named company is a proposal to the owner first."
  ],
